# Sound heard by a person: the one check no machine can make.
scenario: SND-EAR-01
title: Speaker sound by ear
area: Sound
rows: F-SND-01, F-SND-04
machines: any
needs: person
prereq: Speakers or headphones are connected and switched on. Keep the volume low at the start.
step: Open Settings, then Sound. Under Output choose the built-in speakers (or the plugged-in headphones).
expect: The chosen output is marked as in use and the volume slider is shown.
clause: F-SND-01.output
step: Press Play test tone.
expect: You hear two soft notes, the first from the left, the second from the right, with no crackle, no hiss and no gap.
  The two notes must not be cut short.
clause: F-SND-01.tone
step: Move the volume slider from the lowest to the highest position in four steps, pressing Play test tone each time.
expect: Each step is clearly louder than the one before. At the lowest position the tone is quiet but still audible. There is no sudden jump.
clause: F-SND-04.volume
step: Press the mute key (or the Mute button) while the tone plays, then press it again.
expect: The sound stops at once, the icon shows muted, and the tone is heard again after the second press at the old volume.
clause: F-SND-04.mute
